<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="Wars of the Roses">
  <data key="d0">Wars of the Roses</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Wars of the Roses were a series of civil wars fought for control of the English throne between the houses of Lancaster and York during the 15th century.&lt;SEP&gt;The Wars of the Roses were a series of dynastic civil wars in England fought between the houses of Lancaster and York for the English throne from 1455 to 1485.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfa85355242315f033b4bb60edaa01d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10e57cd1e078760fff38d084350f5e77</data>
  <data key="d4">wars_of_the_roses.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1774834671</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="House of Lancaster">
  <data key="d0">House of Lancaster</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The House of Lancaster was one of the two rival factions involved in the Wars of the Roses, represented by the red rose emblem.&lt;SEP&gt;The House of Lancaster is one of the two rival factions in the Wars of the Roses, associated with the red rose and the claim to the English throne.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfa85355242315f033b4bb60edaa01d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10e57cd1e078760fff38d084350f5e77</data>
  <data key="d4">wars_of_the_roses.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1774834671</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="House of York">
  <data key="d0">House of York</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The House of York was the rival faction to the House of Lancaster in the Wars of the Roses, symbolized by the white rose emblem.&lt;SEP&gt;The House of York is the rival faction to the House of Lancaster in the Wars of the Roses, identified by the white rose and also claiming the English throne.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfa85355242315f033b4bb60edaa01d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10e57cd1e078760fff38d084350f5e77</data>
  <data key="d4">wars_of_the_roses.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1774834672</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Henry VI">
  <data key="d0">Henry VI</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Henry VI was the King of England during the Wars of the Roses who experienced periods of madness, affecting his reign and leading to civil unrest.&lt;SEP&gt;Henry VI was the King of England during the Wars of the Roses, known for his periods of madness and being dominated by his queen, Margaret of Anjou.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfa85355242315f033b4bb60edaa01d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10e57cd1e078760fff38d084350f5e77</data>
  <data key="d4">wars_of_the_roses.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1774834672</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Margaret of Anjou">
  <data key="d0">Margaret of Anjou</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Margaret of Anjou was the queen consort of Henry VI and played a significant role in the politics of the Wars of the Roses, dominating Henry VI during his madness.&lt;SEP&gt;Margaret of Anjou was the queen of Henry VI, who played a significant role in the conflicts of the Wars of the Roses and led her faction against the Yorkists.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfa85355242315f033b4bb60edaa01d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10e57cd1e078760fff38d084350f5e77</data>
  <data key="d4">wars_of_the_roses.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1774834672</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Richard, Duke of York">
  <data key="d0">Richard, Duke of York</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Richard, Duke of York was a key figure in the Wars of the Roses who started the conflict through his claim to the throne and role as protector of the realm.&lt;SEP&gt;Richard, Duke of York was a key figure in the Wars of the Roses, serving as protector of the realm and leading the Yorkist forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfa85355242315f033b4bb60edaa01d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10e57cd1e078760fff38d084350f5e77</data>
  <data key="d4">wars_of_the_roses.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1774834672</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Richard III">
  <data key="d0">Richard III</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Richard III was the last king of the House of York, defeated by Henry Tudor at the Battle of Bosworth Field, marking the end of the Wars of the Roses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfa85355242315f033b4bb60edaa01d2</data>
  <data key="d4">wars_of_the_roses.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1774834672</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Edward IV">
  <data key="d0">Edward IV</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Edward IV was the son of Richard, Duke of York, who became king and united the claims of Lancaster and York through his marriage to Elizabeth of York.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfa85355242315f033b4bb60edaa01d2</data>
  <data key="d4">wars_of_the_roses.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1774834672</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lambert Simnel">
  <data key="d0">Lambert Simnel</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lambert Simnel was a pretender to the English throne who represented a Yorkist rising against Henry VII.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfa85355242315f033b4bb60edaa01d2</data>
  <data key="d4">wars_of_the_roses.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1774834672</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battle of Bosworth Field">
  <data key="d0">Battle of Bosworth Field</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Battle of Bosworth Field was the decisive conflict that ended the Wars of the Roses, where Henry Tudor defeated Richard III.&lt;SEP&gt;The Battle of Bosworth Field was the decisive battle in 1485 that ended the Wars of the Roses with the defeat of Richard III.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfa85355242315f033b4bb60edaa01d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10e57cd1e078760fff38d084350f5e77</data>
  <data key="d4">wars_of_the_roses.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1774834672</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battle of St. Albans">
  <data key="d0">Battle of St. Albans</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Battle of St. Albans, fought in 1455, was the first battle of the Wars of the Roses, resulting in a Yorkist victory.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfa85355242315f033b4bb60edaa01d2</data>
  <data key="d4">wars_of_the_roses.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1774834672</data>
