<edge source="Anglo-American Law" target="Civil Law">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Anglo-American law and civil law offer contrasting approaches to property definitions and protections, reflecting different historical contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil Law's reluctance to recognize intangible interests contrasts with Anglo-American Law's broader recognition of possessory rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil law contrasts with Anglo-American law in its treatment of ownership and possession, particularly regarding temporal divisions.</data>
  <data key="d9">legal differences,legal systems,legal traditions,property definitions,property ownership,property rights</data>
